  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["U1", "U2"],
      "pins": ["U1.5", "U1.6", "U2.26", "U2.27"],
      "nets": ["I2C2_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC"],
      "observed": "On the Power sheet, the INA219AIDCNR (U1) SCL (pin 5) and SDA (pin 6) are tied to I2C2_SCL_FCC / I2C2_SDA_FCC with its address note 'I2C address: 0x40'. On the FCC Peripherals sheet, the PCA9685PW (U2) SCL (pin 26) and SDA (pin 27) are tied to the same nets I2C2_SCL_FCC / I2C2_SDA_FCC, also with 'I2C address: 0x40' (all A0–A5 straps shown to GND). Meanwhile I2C3_SCL_FCC / I2C3_SDA_FCC have their own pull-ups (R13, R14) on the FCC sheet but no peripheral attached.",
      "expected": "Two devices that share the same I2C address (0x40) must not sit on the same bus; the spec lists both the INA219 and the PCA9685 at I2C addr 0x40, so they were intended to live on separate buses (e.g. the PCA9685 on the otherwise-empty I2C3_FCC) or be configured to distinct addresses.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet: U1 INA219AIDCNR, pin5 SCL -> I2C2_SCL_FCC, pin6 SDA -> I2C2_SDA_FCC, 'I2C address: 0x40'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "FCC Peripherals sheet: U2 PCA9685PW, pin26 SCL -> I2C2_SCL_FCC, pin27 SDA -> I2C2_SDA_FCC, 'I2C address: 0x40'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Current/voltage sensor | ... | TI INA219AIDCNR, I2C addr 0x40 ... PWM/servo driver | ... | NXP PCA9685PW ... I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "Both the power/telemetry sensor and the 16-channel servo driver answer to address 0x40 on the same I2C2_FCC bus, so the FCC cannot address them independently; transactions intended for one device will be acknowledged by both, corrupting current/voltage readings and servo/PWM control.",
      "confidence": 0.6
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic otherwise matches the spec (the barometer RESET/EOC swap is the documented V1 bug, not an anomaly), but the INA219 and the PCA9685 are both wired to I2C2_FCC at the identical address 0x40, an address collision on a shared bus that the intended design could not have had."
}

